  "notes": "This is the deliverable form and the hardest layout. Every QW-350 welding variable appears TWICE on one row: an Actual Value transcribed from the raw documents, and a Qualified Range *derived* from it by Section IX rules. The flat text layer interleaves the two columns beyond recovery -- dumping page 1 as text yields the labels first and then both columns' values jumbled together -- so each cell is located by intersecting the column-header anchor (x) with the row-label anchor (y). That intersection is the column association the text stream destroys, and it is why RegionSpec carries independent x and y anchors. Not yet mapped: 'Laboratory test no.' (needed by the Class 1 check that the lab report number cited here matches the actual Star Wire report) and the signature blocks. Both need offsets measured before they can be added honestly.",
